如今，“地铁系列”的一些难忘时刻在网上成了梗，尤其是那句高潮台词

429
00:21:55.890 --> 00:21:59.710
delivered by movie me to movie Paige, right before their big kiss.
由电影里的我向电影里的佩姬说出，就在他们热吻之前。

430
00:22:00.310 --> 00:22:02.090
You can't hit a home run if there's
如果没有本垒可以跑向，

431
00:22:02.090 --> 00:22:03.050
no home to run to.
你就无法打出全垒打。

432
00:22:03.870 --> 00:22:08.350
As with anything popular, debates rage online about whether that line is a rom-com
正如任何热门事物一样，网上也充满了争论，这句台词究竟是浪漫喜剧的

433
00:22:08.350 --> 00:22:11.410
classic or absolute flaming shit.
经典还是彻头彻尾的垃圾。

434
00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:13.570
But that's how I felt about Paige.
但这就是我对佩姬的感觉。

435
00:22:14.010 --> 00:22:16.010
Right away, she was home.
一见她，就如同回到了家。

436
00:22:17.250 --> 00:22:21.950
Subway series became a part of our story, an iconic commemoration of our meet cute.
“地铁系列”成为了我们故事的一部分，是我们浪漫初遇的标志性纪念。

437
00:22:22.490 --> 00:22:23.610
Whenever Paige and I
每当我和佩姬

438
00:22:23.610 --> 00:22:29.330
hit a rough patch, I always had Subway series in my back pocket, my get-out-of-jail-free card,
遇到感情危机，我总能把“地铁系列”搬出来当杀手锏，当作我的免死金牌，

439
00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:33.550
a love letter to my wife that somehow became a big hit movie.
这是一封写给我妻子的情书，却阴差阳错成了一部大热电影。

440
00:22:36.060 --> 00:22:41.140
Paige, I hate Subway series.
佩姬，我讨厌“地铁系列”。

441
00:22:42.020 --> 00:22:43.520
I've never told this to anyone.
我从来没对任何人说过这件事。

442
00:22:43.900 --> 00:22:44.800
How could I?
我怎么能说呢？

443
00:22:45.160 --> 00:22:47.800
What woman wouldn't want their partner to write a hit
哪个女人会不希望自己的伴侣为她写一部热门的

444
00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:50.120
rom-com inspired by her?
受她启发而创作的浪漫喜剧呢？

445
00:22:50.620 --> 00:22:52.300
Look, I love Rob.
听着，我爱罗布。

446
00:22:52.620 --> 00:22:56.980
I love his enthusiasm, even when it flirts with cheesiness.
我爱他的热情，哪怕这种热情偶尔边缘擦球、略显老套。

447
00:22:57.360 --> 00:23:05.280
And I love the idea of this movie being for me, which is why I've kept my mouth shut for two decades.
我也喜欢这部电影是专属于我的这种设定，这也是为什么我二十年来一直守口如瓶。

448
00:23:05.980 --> 00:23:09.020
But the truth is, I can barely sit through it.
但事实是，我几乎坐立难安地看完全片。

449
00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:13.280
Rob likes to say it's a love letter to me, but is it?
罗布总喜欢说这是写给我的情书，但真的是吗？

450
00:23:13.280 --> 00:23:19.260
If you look closely, Subway series is not really for, or about, me at all.
如果你仔细看，“地铁系列”其实根本不是为了我，也不是关于我的。

451
00:23:20.400 --> 00:23:25.560
Sure, Rob and I are both big Mets fans, and baseball is a part of how we met and fell in love.
当然，罗b和我都是大都会队的超级粉丝，棒球是我们相识并相爱的一部分。

452
00:23:25.800 --> 00:23:30.100
For our first anniversary, he bought me a customized Bernschitz Brewers jersey,
在我们的第一个结婚纪念日，他给我买了一件定制的伯恩希茨酿酒人队球衣，

453
00:23:30.360 --> 00:23:33.800
which is still, to this day, my single favorite possession.
直到今天，它依然是我最珍视的个人物品。

454
00:23:34.180 --> 00:23:35.840
And we both hated the Yankees.
而且我们两个都讨厌洋基队。

455
00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:38.480
Mets fans are legally required to hate the Yankees.
大都会队的球迷按法律规定必须讨厌洋基队。

456
00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:38.940
Look it up.
不信去查查看。

457
00:23:38.980 --> 00:23:39.800
It's in the Constitution.
宪法里写着呢。

458
00:23:39.800 --> 00:23:45.160
The Mets have won a grand total of two World Series.
大都会队总共才赢得过两次世界大赛冠军。

459
00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:47.820
The Yankees have won 27.
而洋基队赢了27次。

460
00:23:47.940 --> 00:23:49.660
We get to be bitter.
我们有资格感到不甘。

461
00:23:49.860 --> 00:23:51.640
It's all we have.
我们只有这个了。

462
00:23:52.380 --> 00:23:58.400
But in the movie, Rob made the me character a Yankees fan.
但在电影里，罗b把以我为原型的角色改成了一个洋基球迷。

463
00:23:58.820 --> 00:24:00.460
What the fuck?
搞什么鬼？

464
00:24:00.820 --> 00:24:03.440
To a Mets fan, that's sacrilege.
对大都会球迷来说，这是大逆不道。

465
00:24:03.860 --> 00:24:08.240
Plus, Rob never even showed me the script until after it was sold.
况且，罗b直到剧本卖出后才给我看剧本。

466
00:24:08.240 --> 00:24:13.020
When I finally read it, I asked, wait, why am I a Yankees fan?
当我终于读完时，我问，等等，为什么我是洋基球迷？

467
00:24:13.540 --> 00:24:15.960
Oh, I needed to do that, he said,
噢，我得这么写，他说，

468
00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:17.200
to add conflict.
为了增加戏剧冲突。

469
00:24:17.840 --> 00:24:20.280
Oh, well, you succeeded, I frowned.
哦，好吧，你成功了，我皱眉道。

470
00:24:20.440 --> 00:24:22.680
Why couldn't you be the Yankees fan?
为什么你不能当洋基球迷？

471
00:24:23.160 --> 00:24:27.140
Of course, we both knew the real answer, because Yankees fans are assholes.
当然，我们俩都知道真正的答案，因为洋基球迷都是混蛋。

472
00:24:27.460 --> 00:24:28.780
Sorry, but they are.
抱歉，但他们确实是。

473
00:24:29.100 --> 00:24:34.400
Yankees fans are the lazy, entitled nobility to Mets fans' humble, hardworking peasantry.
相比于大都会球迷卑微、勤劳的平民阶层，洋基球迷就是懒惰、享有特权的贵族。

474
00:24:34.400 --> 00:24:36.940
The Yankees are Marie Antoinette.
洋基队就是玛丽·安托瓦内特。

475
00:24:37.180 --> 00:24:38.580
The Mets are Joan of Arc.
大都会队则是圣女贞德。

476
00:24:39.460 --> 00:24:41.600
I'll ask Nigel if we can switch it,
我会问问奈杰尔我们能不能改回来，

477
00:24:41.680 --> 00:24:42.060
Rob said.
罗b说。

478
00:24:42.320 --> 00:24:42.800
No big deal.
这没什么大不了的。

479
00:24:43.300 --> 00:24:44.440
But guess what happened?
但你猜怎么着？

480
00:24:45.180 --> 00:24:46.220
Have you guessed yet?
你猜到了吗？

481
00:24:46.520 --> 00:24:47.680
It never got switched.
根本就没改。

482
00:24:48.120 --> 00:24:51.880
He later said Nigel preferred the woman as a Yankees fan.
他后来改口说奈杰尔更希望那个女性角色是洋基球迷。

483
00:24:52.280 --> 00:24:53.340
Why, you ask?
你问为什么？

484
00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:54.560
I never got an
我从来没有得到过

485
00:24:54.560 --> 00:24:55.080
explanation.
任何解释。

486
00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:57.980
Because there isn't one.
因为根本就没有。

487
00:24:58.460 --> 00:25:03.020
The truth is, I'm not convinced Rob ever even pitched the idea
事实是，我甚至不相信罗b真的提出过

488
00:25:03.020 --> 00:25:04.040
of switching it.
要改这个主意。

489
00:25:04.920 --> 00:25:12.080
The most quoted line from Subway series is, you can't hit a home run if there's no
《地铁大战》中最经典的一句台词是，如果没有本垒可以跑，你就打不出本垒打。

490
00:25:12.080 --> 00:25:13.220
home to run to.
所以，在这个设定中，女性就是本垒板，她所有的工作就是待在那里，

491
00:25:14.100 --> 00:25:22.300
So, in this formulation, the woman is home plate, and her whole job is to just wait
等待男性完成他的胜利慢跑。

492
00:25:22.300 --> 00:25:24.420
there for the man to complete his victory trot.
然后，踩在她身上？

493
00:25:24.560 --> 00:25:26.280
Then, step on her?
因为这可真不怎么地。

494
00:25:26.800 --> 00:25:27.940
Because that's not great.
电影上映时，海报上的宣传语是，她是个好球，但其中另有玄机。

495
00:25:29.140 --> 00:25:35.980
When the movie came out, the tagline on the poster was, she was a catch, but there was a catch.
没错，玄机就是，她是个该死的洋基球迷。

496
00:25:36.960 --> 00:25:40.140
Yeah, the catch is, she's a damn Yankees fan.
而且，这个角色跟我一点也不像。

497
00:25:40.720 --> 00:25:43.140
Also, the character is nothing like me.
她比我

498
00:25:43.380 --> 00:25:44.600
She's much nicer
好太多了。

499
00:25:44.600 --> 00:25:45.020
than me.
我这话可不是在夸她。

500
00:25:45.180 --> 00:25:47.060
And I don't mean that as a compliment.
我这话可不是在夸奖。

501
00:25:47.360 --> 00:25:50.820
She feels less like an actual woman and more like
她感觉不太像一个真正的女人，而更像是

502
00:25:50.820 --> 00:25:52.360
a woman written by a man.
一个由男人笔下写出来的女人。

503
00:25:52.920 --> 00:25:54.400
I'll do respect to Rob.
我会尊重罗布。

504
00:25:54.520 --> 00:25:55.540
I know he meant well.
我知道他是好意。

505
00:25:56.200 --> 00:25:57.780
Everything she does is in
她所做的一切都是在

506
00:25:57.780 --> 00:25:59.160
reaction to the man.
对男人的反应。

507
00:25:59.540 --> 00:26:04.180
Being charmed, rolling her eyes, getting mad for giving, all reactive.
被迷住、翻白眼、因为付出而生气，全都是被动作出反应。

508
00:26:04.920 --> 00:26:08.480
Based on a true love story, the poster claimed.
海报上声称，改编自一个真实的爱情故事。

509
00:26:08.840 --> 00:26:11.720
So then, the whole world started asking me,
所以当时，全世界都开始问我，

510
00:26:11.720 --> 00:26:14.840
how does it feel to see yourself on the big screen?
在银幕上看到自己是什么感觉？

511
00:26:15.260 --> 00:26:18.340
And I wanted to say, I have no idea.
而我想说的是，我毫无头绪。

512
00:26:18.340 --> 00:26:18.680
It's not
那根本

513
00:26:18.680 --> 00:26:19.140
really me.
不是我。

514
00:26:19.240 --> 00:26:20.360
I don't even like that chick.
我甚至不喜欢那个妞。

515
00:26:20.700 --> 00:26:21.760
But I couldn't.
但我没能说出口。

516
00:26:22.500 --> 00:26:24.640
By the time the movie came out, Emmett
电影上映的时候，埃梅特

517
00:26:24.640 --> 00:26:25.080
was born.
出生了。

518
00:26:25.300 --> 00:26:28.580
So, simultaneously, Rob had two babies.
所以，罗布同时有了两个孩子。

519
00:26:29.000 --> 00:26:32.580
One, a sparkly hit rom-com that made him the toast of
一个是闪耀的爱情喜剧热门之作，让他成为了

520
00:26:32.580 --> 00:26:32.960
Hollywood.
好莱坞的宠儿。

521
00:26:33.360 --> 00:26:36.720
The other, a complicated mystery with an uncertain future.
另一个是一个前途未卜、复杂的谜团。

522
00:26:37.340 --> 00:26:39.100
It should come as no surprise
毫无疑问

523
00:26:39.100 --> 00:26:40.900
which one he leaned into more.
他更倾向于哪一个。

524
00:26:41.440 --> 00:26:45.620
Rob, Nigel, and the cast traveled the globe to promote Subway series.
罗布、奈杰尔和演员们环游世界去宣传《地铁系列》。

525
00:26:45.880 --> 00:26:49.440
At every press junket, Rob said I was his inspiration.
在每一次新闻发布会上，罗布都说我是他的灵感来源。

526
00:26:49.900 --> 00:26:51.800
And the reporters and screening
而记者和观影

527
00:26:51.800 --> 00:26:54.400
audiences would all go, oh.
观众们都会发出“哦”的惊叹。

528
00:26:55.300 --> 00:26:58.440
But I did not feel like an inspiration.
但我一点也不觉得自己是灵感来源。

529
00:26:59.020 --> 00:27:02.080
I was the new mother of a baby I did not
我成了一个新生儿的母亲，而我对这个孩子并没有

530
00:27:02.080 --> 00:27:03.120
fully understand.
完全理解。

531
00:27:03.540 --> 00:27:06.780
Living in a city in which I felt all alone.
住在一个让我感到无比孤独的城市里。

532
00:27:07.240 --> 00:27:09.800
Watching my husband's fever for success
看着我丈夫对成功的狂热

533
00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:13.320
burn hotter than ever now that we had a special needs child.
比以往任何时候都烧得更旺，因为我们现在有了一个特殊需求儿童。

534
00:27:14.080 --> 00:27:16.520
Rob felt he had to become a super
罗布觉得他必须成为一个超级

535
00:27:16.520 --> 00:27:19.020
provider to support Emmett for his entire life.
顶梁柱，以支持埃梅特的一生。

536
00:27:19.760 --> 00:27:24.140
The thing is, Rob was a full-on workaholic even before
问题是，罗布在埃梅特出生前

537
00:27:24.140 --> 00:27:25.120
Emmett's birth.
就是一个十足的工作狂。

538
00:27:25.700 --> 00:27:32.320
But now, our baby's needs gave him a free pass to not only continue working non-stop,
但现在，我们孩子的需求给了他一张通行证，让他不仅可以继续不间断地、

539
00:27:32.520 --> 00:27:36.960
obsessively, but to do it all under this cloak of nobility.
执着地工作，而且这一切都有了高尚的外衣。

540
00:27:37.460 --> 00:27:39.540
He was the hero, the breadwinner.
他是英雄，是顶梁柱。

541
00:27:40.500 --> 00:27:46.640
Rob loved Emmett, but he also wanted to be off having immersive adventures in imaginary lands,
罗布爱埃梅特，但他也想去虚构的世界里进行沉浸式的冒险，

542
00:27:46.840 --> 00:27:52.340
escaping the hard day-to-day realities I had to confront, mostly on my own.
逃避我不得不面对的残酷日常现实，而这些大多只能由我一个人承担。

543
00:27:53.180 --> 00:28:03.040
At such a lost, lonely moment for me, watching Subway series, this shiny, happy rom-com populated by
在我如此迷茫、孤独的时刻，看着《地铁系列》这部由

544
00:28:03.040 --> 00:28:07.460
beautiful young actors with fake accents, none of them were real New Yorkers.
说着假口音的美丽年轻演员主演的光鲜亮丽的快乐爱情喜剧，他们全都不是真正的纽约人。

545
00:28:07.880 --> 00:28:10.480
Felt like seeing a mirage
感觉就像是在沙漠中看到了

546
00:28:10.480 --> 00:28:17.820
in the desert, a strange hallucination born of thirSt. None of it resembled my real life.
海市蜃楼，一种由渴望诞生的奇异幻觉。这一切都不像我的真实生活。

547
00:28:18.160 --> 00:28:18.920
Not anymore.
不再像了。

548
00:28:18.920 --> 00:28:24.120
It felt like the funhouse mirror version of a life I'd left behind.
感觉就像是我已经抛下的生活的哈哈镜版本。

549
00:28:24.500 --> 00:28:27.020
A fairy tale about two young
一个关于两个没有责任、

550
00:28:27.020 --> 00:28:32.700
people with no responsibilities, no crushing parental weight on their shoulders.
肩膀上没有沉重父母负担的年轻人的童话故事。

551
00:28:33.160 --> 00:28:35.180
Nothing but free time to
有的是时间

552
00:28:35.180 --> 00:28:39.980
obsess over baseball and drink beer and eat hot dogs and never gain weight.
沉迷棒球、喝啤酒、吃热狗，还永远吃不胖。

553
00:28:40.540 --> 00:28:42.500
This is why rom-coms are such
这就是为什么浪漫喜剧

554
00:28:42.500 --> 00:28:43.740
an irresponsible genre.
是如此不负责任的类型片。

555
00:28:44.080 --> 00:28:49.180
They make us chase illusions, then feel bored and sad once we catch them.
它们让我们追逐幻觉，一旦追到又觉得无聊和悲伤。

556
00:28:49.760 --> 00:28:50.820
God bless them.
愿上帝保佑它们。

557
00:28:51.300 --> 00:28:53.320
Rob is the gooey dreamer in our relationship.
罗伯是我们这段关系里那个满脑子幻想的浪漫主义者。

558
00:28:53.320 --> 00:28:54.320
I'm the pragmatiSt.
我则是那个现实主义者。

559
00:28:54.720 --> 00:28:59.480
The rom-com era of my life, if I'd ever had one, was over.
我人生的浪漫喜剧时代，如果我曾有过的话，已经结束了。

560
00:29:00.480 --> 00:29:01.160
No.
不。

561
00:29:01.500 --> 00:29:06.100
The movie I wanted to see now was the one that happens after the credits.
我现在想看的电影是演完职员表之后发生的故事。

562
00:29:06.540 --> 00:29:08.560
After the big proposal
在那个盛大的求婚之后

563
00:29:08.560 --> 00:29:10.440
on the center field jumbotron.
在中场大屏幕上。

564
00:29:10.700 --> 00:29:14.940
After the charming, light-hearted characters get hit by a real-life
在那些迷人、轻松的角色遭遇现实生活中的

565
00:29:14.940 --> 00:29:15.700
wrecking ball.
重锤之后。

566
00:29:16.220 --> 00:29:16.540
Shattered.
粉碎。

567
00:29:17.180 --> 00:29:17.860
Pulverized.
碾压。

568
00:29:18.140 --> 00:29:22.020
Forced to gather up the tiny pieces of their former selves
被迫收拾他们过去的零星碎片

569
00:29:22.020 --> 00:29:24.340
and glue them into something new.
把它们粘合成新的东西。

570
00:29:24.700 --> 00:29:28.640
Letting go, forever, of the perfect lives they'd planned on
永远放弃他们曾计划拥有

571
00:29:28.640 --> 00:29:28.940
having.
的完美生活。

572
00:29:29.820 --> 00:29:31.760
That's the movie I wanted to see.
那才是我想看的电影。

573
00:29:32.740 --> 00:29:35.060
But Hollywood doesn't make that kind of movie.
但好莱坞不拍这种电影。

574
00:29:36.440 --> 00:29:38.700
So, I wrote it as a book instead.
所以，我把它写成了一本书。

575
00:29:41.330 --> 00:29:41.770
Darcy.
达西。

576
00:29:42.990 --> 00:29:45.070
I'm barely in my mom's book.
我妈的书里几乎没怎么写我。

577
00:29:45.470 --> 00:29:46.870
That should tell you everything.
这就足以说明一切了。

578
00:29:47.770 --> 00:29:51.290
I hate to be the cliche sibling of a child with a disability.
我讨厌成为那种身有残疾的孩子的陈词滥调式的手足。

579
00:29:51.850 --> 00:29:53.050
But when you're a kid,
但当你还是个孩子的时候，

580
00:29:53.210 --> 00:29:58.350
and you get less attention than your brother, and you don't fully understand why, it's hard.
得到的关注比哥哥少，而且你并不完全明白为什么，这很难受。

581
00:29:59.330 --> 00:30:01.950
It took me a while to realize Emmett was different.
我花了很长时间才意识到埃米特与众不同。

582
00:30:02.670 --> 00:30:05.790
Around age six, I noticed that kids sometimes made
大约六岁的时候，我发现有时孩子们会

583
00:30:05.790 --> 00:30:06.270
fun of him.
取笑他。

584
00:30:06.910 --> 00:30:09.310
Then I heard this weird word I didn't know.
然后我听到了这个我不懂的奇怪词汇。

585
00:30:09.970 --> 00:30:12.130
Before that word, my brother was just my
在那词出现之前，我哥哥就只是我

586
00:30:12.130 --> 00:30:12.410
brother.
哥哥。

587
00:30:13.030 --> 00:30:13.590
Funny.
有趣。

588
00:30:14.090 --> 00:30:14.630
Silly.
滑稽。

589
00:30:15.030 --> 00:30:16.770
A bit eccentric, I guess.
我猜，有点古怪。

590
00:30:17.230 --> 00:30:18.450
But normal to me.
但在我看来很正常。

591
00:30:19.030 --> 00:30:21.350
If he was being annoying, I'd say,
如果他惹我烦了，我会说，

592
00:30:21.570 --> 00:30:23.130
stop, Emmett, you're being annoying.
住手，埃米特，你真烦人。

593
00:30:23.910 --> 00:30:25.950
But mostly I just looked up to him.
但大多数时候我都很崇拜他。

594
00:30:26.330 --> 00:30:27.590
He was my big bro.
他是我好哥哥。

595
00:30:28.590 --> 00:30:32.650
Then, one day on the school bus, he was a retard.
然后，有一天在校车上，他成了个智障。

596
00:30:33.690 --> 00:30:35.710
I asked my parents what that meant.
我问父母那是什么意思。

597
00:30:36.230 --> 00:30:38.550
I'll never forget the looks on their faces.
我永远不会忘记他们脸上的表情。

598
00:30:39.350 --> 00:30:42.110
Gutted, but also like they'd been waiting for it.
痛彻心扉，但也像是早就料到这一天会来。

599
00:30:42.770 --> 00:30:47.210
They said sometimes bullies used that word to be mean to people like my brother.
他们说，有时恶霸会用这个词来对付像我哥哥这样的人。

600
00:30:48.070 --> 00:30:50.410
Why would anyone want to be mean to Emmett?
为什么会有人想对埃米特恶语相向呢？

601
00:30:50.590 --> 00:30:51.470
I asked.
我问过。

602
00:30:52.230 --> 00:30:54.870
Because he's different, they said.
因为他与众不同，他们说。

603
00:30:55.510 --> 00:31:00.230
And that's when my parents gave me an in-depth description of what it really means to have
就在那时，我的父母向我详细解释了

604
00:31:00.230 --> 00:31:00.890
Down syndrome.
唐氏综合征究竟意味着什么。

605
00:31:01.270 --> 00:31:06.690
The medical issues, the learning challenges, the social differences, and how it
医疗问题、学习障碍、社交差异，以及这如何

606
00:31:06.690 --> 00:31:08.210
can make you a target for bullies.
会让你成为霸凌的目标。

607
00:31:09.110 --> 00:31:10.990
I was so pissed.
我当时气极了。

608
00:31:11.530 --> 00:31:12.570
Emmett was unique.
埃mett是独一无二的。

609
00:31:12.810 --> 00:31:14.250
He was his own song.
他有他自己的节拍。

610
00:31:14.610 --> 00:31:17.110
If people couldn't hear it, then fuck them.
如果别人听不懂，那他们就去死吧。

611
00:31:17.930 --> 00:31:21.550
On that day, I anointed myself my brother's protector.
从那一天起，我自封为我哥哥的保护神。

612
00:31:22.290 --> 00:31:27.730
Emmett's kid sister, half a decade younger, this little pipsqueak full of piss and vinegar,
作为埃mett小了五岁的妹妹，这个充满反叛精神的小不点儿，

613
00:31:27.730 --> 00:31:30.490
fending off the bullies, making a scene.
击退霸凌者，大闹一场。

614
00:31:30.890 --> 00:31:31.990
The louder, the better.
动静越大越好。

615
00:31:32.910 --> 00:31:34.330
Once, when I was eight,
有一次，在我八岁的时候，

616
00:31:34.590 --> 00:31:38.790
I stood up on my seat and announced to the entire bus that Deven O'Shields,
我站到座位上，向全车人宣布，德文·奥希尔兹，

617
00:31:39.110 --> 00:31:41.990
who'd been blowing spitballs at a fast asleep Emmett,
那个一直朝正酣睡的埃mett吐纸团的人，

618
00:31:42.150 --> 00:31:45.510
he always falls asleep in moving vehicles, still does,
他坐车总是会睡着，现在也是，

619
00:31:45.510 --> 00:31:48.910
was a fascist motherfucker who must be stopped.
是个必须被制止的法西斯混蛋。

620
00:31:49.970 --> 00:31:53.050
My parents beamed with pride as I regaled them with
当我向他们讲述我的英勇事迹时，

621
00:31:53.050 --> 00:31:54.070
my tale of bravery.
我的父母骄傲得合不拢嘴。

622
00:31:54.730 --> 00:31:58.050
They quote that line to this day to describe all kinds of people,
直到今天，他们还在引用那句话来形容各种人，

623
00:31:58.310 --> 00:32:01.850
from drivers who don't use their turn signal to certain U.S.
从不打转向灯的司机到某些美国

624
00:32:02.010 --> 00:32:02.310
presidents.
总统。

625
00:32:03.450 --> 00:32:05.970
Hell yeah, they said, high-fiving me.
太对了，他们说，与我击掌相庆。

626
00:32:06.530 --> 00:32:09.390
I can still remember my mother squeezing me tight,
我至今仍记得母亲紧紧地把我搂在怀里，

627
00:32:09.390 --> 00:32:16.290
whispering in my ear, Darcy, we are so lucky you're our daughter, and Emmett is so lucky you're his
在我耳边低语，达西，我们有你这样的女儿真是太幸运了，埃mett有你这样的

628
00:32:16.290 --> 00:32:16.650
sister.
姐姐真是太幸运了。

629
00:32:17.550 --> 00:32:19.430
I finally had their attention.
我终于得到了他们的关注。

630
00:32:19.750 --> 00:32:21.410
I finally had a thing.
我终于有了一技之长。

631
00:32:21.970 --> 00:32:24.490
Now, instead of living in Emmett's
现在，我不再活在埃mett的

632
00:32:24.490 --> 00:32:27.150
shadow, I was Emmett's bodyguard.
阴影下，而是成了埃mett的保镖。

633
00:32:28.130 --> 00:32:32.090
Basking in my own glory, I climbed up to my favorite spot,
沐浴在自己的荣光中，我爬上了我最喜欢的地方，

634
00:32:32.410 --> 00:32:34.070
the treehouse in our backyard.
我们后院的树屋。

635
00:32:35.130 --> 00:32:37.250
It was Emmett's favorite spot, too.
这也是埃mett最喜欢的地方。

636
00:32:37.790 --> 00:32:39.310
Whenever we played hide and
小时候我们玩捉迷藏时，

637
00:32:39.310 --> 00:32:45.170
seek as kids, he would announce, I'm going to hide in the treehouse, which kind of defeated the
他总是大喊，我要藏在树屋里，这其实违背了

638
00:32:45.170 --> 00:32:48.110
whole hide-and-seek concept, but was also classic Emmett.
捉迷藏的真谛，但也十分符合埃mett的风格。

639
00:32:48.550 --> 00:32:51.290
He simply couldn't lie, still can't.
他根本不会撒谎，现在也不会。

640
00:32:52.290 --> 00:32:53.850
Emmett climbed up to find me.
埃mett爬上来找我。

641
00:32:54.550 --> 00:32:56.850
Hey, I said, still aglow.
嘿，我说着，余热未消。

642
00:32:57.730 --> 00:33:00.350
Hey, he said, climbing in next to me.
嘿，他说着，在我身旁坐下。

643
00:33:01.150 --> 00:33:05.090
Listen, Darcy, don't do that anymore, okay?
听着，达西，以后别那样了好吗？

644
00:33:05.930 --> 00:33:07.030
Don't do what?
别哪样？

645
00:33:07.650 --> 00:33:08.890
Stick up for me.
为我出头。

646
00:33:09.690 --> 00:33:10.330
What?
什么？

647
00:33:10.590 --> 00:33:11.610
I exclaimed.
我惊呼道。

648
00:33:11.950 --> 00:33:14.210
But Devon O'Shields was being a dick.
可是德文·奥希尔兹太混蛋了。

649
00:33:14.750 --> 00:33:17.250
I know, but it doesn't help.
我知道，但这没有用。

650
00:33:17.590 --> 00:33:18.270
You're my
你是我的

651
00:33:18.270 --> 00:33:20.030
little sister, you know?
小妹妹，你知道吗？

652
00:33:21.010 --> 00:33:23.770
I could feel a lump forming in my little throat.
我能感觉到喉咙里哽咽出一个硬块。

653
00:33:24.230 --> 00:33:26.030
I thought I was his hero.
我以为我是他的英雄。

654
00:33:27.070 --> 00:33:31.250
So I have to just sit there and let those assholes fuck with my brother?
所以我只能坐在那里，任由那些混蛋欺负我哥哥？

655
00:33:32.330 --> 00:33:34.050
Somehow I'd been swearing like
不知怎么的，我满嘴脏话就像

656
00:33:34.050 --> 00:33:36.690
a sailor and getting away with it since age five.
个水手一样，而且从五岁起就没挨过收拾。

657
00:33:37.850 --> 00:33:41.350
Emmett smiled at me, gently, like he understood
埃米特对我笑了笑，很温柔，好像他懂

658
00:33:41.350 --> 00:33:42.330
something I didn't.
一些我还不懂的事。

659
00:33:43.150 --> 00:33:43.790
Yes.
是的。

660
00:33:44.830 --> 00:33:50.230
I didn't want to cry, but I started imagining it, watching on and doing
我不想哭，但我开始想象那一幕，眼睁睁看着却无能

661
00:33:50.230 --> 00:33:51.730
nothing as Emmett got bullied.
为力，任由埃米特被欺负。

662
00:33:52.190 --> 00:33:53.690
And my eyes welled up.
然后我的眼泪夺眶而出。

663
00:33:54.090 --> 00:33:55.230
I turned away.
我转过头去。

664
00:33:56.230 --> 00:33:57.850
Fine, I said.
随便吧，我说。

665
00:33:58.250 --> 00:33:59.150
Get beat up.
被打活该。

666
00:33:59.350 --> 00:34:00.450
What do I care?
关我什么事？

667
00:34:01.430 --> 00:34:03.290
Darcy, get out, Emmett.
达西，滚开，埃米特。

668
00:34:03.730 --> 00:34:04.770
