爬了下去。

671
00:34:09.330 --> 00:34:10.970
He never yelled back at me.
他从不对我大喊大叫。

672
00:34:11.250 --> 00:34:12.150
Not once.
一次也没有。

673
00:34:12.370 --> 00:34:13.550
Our entire childhood.
在我们整个童年里。

674
00:34:14.790 --> 00:34:16.690
Things changed after that.
从那以后情况就变了。

675
00:34:17.130 --> 00:34:22.310
I'd gone from being jealous of Emmett to being his protector to being, I didn't know what.
我对埃米特的感情从嫉妒变成保护，再到后来，我也不知道算什么了。

676
00:34:22.310 --> 00:34:23.470
Emmett.
埃米特。

677
00:34:23.470 --> 00:34:28.530
The next day, when Devin O'Shield started picking on Emmett, I kept chatting with my friends,
第二天，当德文·奥谢尔德开始找埃米特麻烦时，我继续和朋友聊天，

678
00:34:29.050 --> 00:34:30.150
pretending I didn't notice.
假装没看见。

679
00:34:31.110 --> 00:34:35.930
Emmett just sat there, looking out the window, peacefully ignoring it.
埃米特只是坐在那里，看着窗外，安详地无视这一切。

680
00:34:36.810 --> 00:34:39.250
Civil disobedience, like Gandhi.
非暴力不合作，就像甘地一样。

681
00:34:40.410 --> 00:34:42.550
Admirable, but not my style.
令人钦佩，但不是我的风格。

682
00:34:43.470 --> 00:34:46.250
That day at lunch, I walked by Devin's
那天午饭时，我从德文的

683
00:34:46.250 --> 00:34:50.430
seat and hawked a big, juicy loogie into his Hawaiian punch when he wasn't looking.
座位旁走过，趁他不注意，往他的夏威夷果汁里吐了一大口浓痰。

684
00:34:51.210 --> 00:34:52.090
Then I
然后我

685
00:34:52.090 --> 00:34:56.430
watched from across the cafeteria, as Devin drank every last drop.
在餐厅的另一头看着德文把每一滴都喝了下去。

686
00:34:57.170 --> 00:34:58.670
I never told anyone,
我从来没告诉过任何人，

687
00:34:58.910 --> 00:35:00.590
and I didn't feel bad about it.
而且我一点也不觉得内疚。

688
00:35:01.150 --> 00:35:04.490
My loogie was the most natural ingredient in that Hawaiian punch.
我的浓痰可以说是那杯夏威夷果汁里最天然的成分了。

689
00:35:05.470 --> 00:35:09.650
It can be weird, having a big brother whose path is so different from yours.
有一个人生道路与你截然不同的哥哥，这种感觉可能会很怪异。

690
00:35:10.230 --> 00:35:15.590
As the neurotypical kid, at first, your parents marvel at every little thing you do.
作为一个神经典型的小孩，起初，你的父母会对你做的每一件小事啧啧称奇。

691
00:35:16.130 --> 00:35:18.650
Look at her stack those blocks so neatly.
看她把积木叠得这么整齐。

692
00:35:19.570 --> 00:35:21.910
You get praise for shit other parents wouldn't
你会因为一些其他父母根本

693
