为什么？

700
00:35:43.110 --> 00:35:45.050
Because you've got this.
因为这些对你来说都是小菜一碟。

701
00:35:45.510 --> 00:35:47.530
You've always had this.
你向来如此。

702
00:35:47.530 --> 00:35:49.570
Your teachers love you.
老师们都很喜欢你。

703
00:35:49.770 --> 00:35:51.490
You do your homework by yourself.
作业都是你自己独立完成。

704
00:35:51.750 --> 00:35:54.290
You don't need speech therapy or open
你不需要语言治疗，也不需要做开

705
00:35:54.290 --> 00:35:54.990
heart surgery.
胸手术。

706
00:35:55.650 --> 00:35:56.630
You're easy.
你很好带。

707
00:35:57.610 --> 00:35:58.990
And there's the rub.
而问题也恰恰出在这里。

708
00:35:59.350 --> 00:36:02.570
You go from miracle child to latchkey kid in the
转眼之间，你从一个奇迹般的孩子变成了

709
00:36:02.570 --> 00:36:03.290
blink of an eye.
无人照管的钥匙儿童。

710
00:36:03.910 --> 00:36:09.130
My once anti-establishment parents had settled down in a wealthy suburb full of cookie
我曾经反叛主流的父母，在富裕的郊区安定了下来，那里到处都是千篇一律的

711
00:36:09.130 --> 00:36:12.850
cutter homes, cookie cutter families, cookie cutter kids.
房屋、千篇一律的家庭和千篇一律的孩子。

712
00:36:13.510 --> 00:36:15.770
They wanted a daughter who fit that picture.
他们想要一个符合那种画面的女儿。

713
00:36:16.530 --> 00:36:20.910
And then, they wanted to put that picture up on the fridge and walk away.
然后，他们只想把这幅画面贴在冰箱上，就撒手不管了。

714
00:36:21.790 --> 00:36:23.270
All those things they were
所有那些如果生下健全孩子

715
00:36:23.270 --> 00:36:26.890
never going to take for granted if they had a non-disabled child?
就绝不会视为理所当然的事物呢？

716
00:36:27.410 --> 00:36:29.150
They totally took them for
他们却把它们完全

717
00:36:29.150 --> 00:36:29.470
granted.
视为理所当然。

718
00:36:30.350 --> 00:36:35.210
But I still had to keep stacking those blocks long after the applause stopped.
但掌声停止后，我还是得继续把那些积木垒下去。

719
00:36:36.130 --> 00:36:36.690
Why?
为什么？

720
00:36:37.310 --> 00:36:37.870
Because
因为

721
00:36:37.870 --> 00:36:43.030
for the first five years of Emmett's life, my parents feared they'd never have a kid who would go to
在埃米特生命的前五年里，我的父母一直害怕他们不会再有一个能上

722
00:36:43.030 --> 00:36:50.390
college, get married, make them grandparents, become a successful, independent grown-up, qualified to one
大学、结婚、让他们抱孙子、成为一个成功独立的成年人、并且有资格在

723
00:36:50.390 --> 00:36:52.430
day do the most important job of all.
未来承担最重要责任的孩子。

724
00:36:53.070 --> 00:36:55.450
Watch over Emmett once they were gone.
等他们离去后，替他们照顾埃米特。

725
00:36:56.450 --> 00:36:58.030
My parents always say they
我父母总说他们

726
00:36:58.030 --> 00:36:59.450
don't want me to feel that pressure.
不希望我感到那种压力。

727
00:36:59.950 --> 00:37:01.070
But it's a lie.
但这是假话。

728
00:37:01.390 --> 00:37:02.990
And it should be a lie.
而且这也本该是假话。

729
00:37:03.530 --> 00:37:04.990
Of course they want me to help
他们当然希望我能在

730
00:37:04.990 --> 00:37:06.510
