他们甚至连问都不问一声。

737
00:37:24.730 --> 00:37:27.730
No, how are the applications going, Darce?
没有问过“达茜，申请情况怎么样了？”

738
00:37:28.530 --> 00:37:29.050
No.
没有。

739
00:37:29.610 --> 00:37:31.190
Need a ride to a campus tour?
没有问过“要不要搭车去参观校园？”

740
00:37:31.970 --> 00:37:32.490
Nothing.
什么都没有。

741
00:37:33.350 --> 00:37:33.770
Nada.
半点没有。

742
00:37:34.330 --> 00:37:34.850
Crickets.
静悄悄的。

743
00:37:35.590 --> 00:37:37.550
They were focused on Emmett and on their
他们的注意力全在埃米特和他们自己

744
00:37:37.550 --> 00:37:38.010
own shit.
那些破事上。

745
00:37:38.470 --> 00:37:41.310
And I was just supposed to keep doing what I'd always done.
而我本该继续做我一直以来都在做的事。

746
00:37:41.790 --> 00:37:43.550
Be the little miracle they
做那个他们可以

747
00:37:43.550 --> 00:37:44.590
could happily ignore.
高高兴兴地置之不理的小奇迹。

748
00:37:45.570 --> 00:37:49.970
When my mom found out her memoir was going to be published, she let Emmett and
当我妈妈得知她的回忆录即将出版时，她让埃米特和

749
00:37:49.970 --> 00:37:53.390
I read the manuscript to make sure we weren't embarrassed by anything.
我阅读了手稿，以确保我们不会对里面的任何内容感到尴尬。

750
00:37:54.350 --> 00:37:56.230
What I read was far worse
而我读到的内容要糟糕得多

751
00:37:56.230 --> 00:37:57.050
than embarrassing.
比尴尬更甚。

752
00:37:57.690 --> 00:38:02.750
It was proof, in print, of what I'd always feared about my place in our family.
那是白纸黑字的证据，证实了我一直以来对自己在家族中地位的恐惧。

753
00:38:03.290 --> 00:38:05.050
I was a side character.
我只是个配角。

754
00:38:05.470 --> 00:38:07.330
The straight man in the comedy.
喜剧里的本分人。

755
00:38:07.690 --> 00:38:09.770
The innocent bystander in the tragedy.
悲剧里的无辜旁观者。

756
00:38:10.170 --> 00:38:12.010
The control group in the experiment.
实验里的对照组。

757
00:38:12.750 --> 00:38:16.650
I was, in my mother's eyes, uncomplicated.
在我母亲眼里，我是个简单的孩子。

758
00:38:17.610 --> 00:38:20.850
Who on earth wants to be thought of as uncomplicated?
世上究竟有谁愿意被当成头脑简单的人呢？

759
00:38:21.390 --> 00:38:24.610
If you look closely, everybody's complicated.
如果你仔细观察，每个人其实都很复杂。

760
00:38:25.670 --> 00:38:28.010
But my parents didn't look closely.
但我的父母并没有仔细观察。

761
00:38:29.170 --> 00:38:32.750
In my mom's defense, I didn't complain much.
为我妈说句公道话，我平时抱怨得确实不多。

762
00:38:33.630 --> 00:38:39.950
Most of my complicated feelings about Emmett, my family, my life, I kept to myself.
我对埃mett、对我的家人、对我的人生那些复杂的感受，我都藏在心里。

763
00:38:40.670 --> 00:38:46.190
My mother wrote a memoir about raising a child who is complicated in a way you don't have to look
我母亲写了一本回忆录，讲的是如何抚养一个孩子，他的复杂无需你费力去

764
00:38:46.190 --> 00:38:46.890
too hard to see.
仔细寻找就能看到。

765
00:38:47.850 --> 00:38:51.030
Emmett is complicated in uncomplicated ways.
埃mett的复杂一目了然。

766
00:38:52.010 --> 00:38:53.650
But all of our brains are
但我们所有人的大脑不都

767
00:38:53.650 --> 00:38:55.030
little meat computers, right?
只是一台装在头骨里的生物计算机吗？

768
00:38:55.830 --> 00:39:00.610
Reading my mom's book, mine ran a count of all the words in it devoted to me.
读我妈的书时，我的大脑自动统计了里面留给我的所有字数。

769
00:39:01.390 --> 00:39:06.550
And those words, excerpted and bound, wouldn't fill a Chipotle menu.
而那些字被摘录并装订起来，连一张Chipotle的菜单都填不满。

770
00:39:07.230 --> 00:39:08.810
Because I'm the easy one,
因为我是那个让人省心的孩子，

771
00:39:08.810 --> 00:39:10.510
if you don't look too hard.
如果你不仔细看的话。

772
00:39:11.370 --> 00:39:14.990
But if you do, you might not like what you see.
但如果你真的仔细看了，你可能就不会喜欢你所看到的了。

773
00:39:15.730 --> 00:39:17.450
Because it's complicated.
因为事情很复杂。

774
00:39:19.850 --> 00:39:20.550
Emmett.
埃mett。

775
00:39:21.810 --> 00:39:23.870
My name is Emmett.
我叫埃mett。

776
00:39:24.050 --> 00:39:26.110
And I have Down Syndrome.
我患有唐氏综合征。

777
00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:30.030
But that is not the most interesting thing about me.
但这并不是我身上最有趣的地方。

778
00:39:30.810 --> 00:39:34.190
Having Down Syndrome is just a part of me.
患有唐氏综合征只是我的一部分。

779
00:39:34.890 --> 00:39:36.370
Like my elbow.
就像我的手肘一样。

780
00:39:36.650 --> 00:39:38.870
Or being allergic to shrimp.
或者对虾过敏。

781
00:39:39.210 --> 00:39:41.450
I'm happy it is a part of me.
我很高兴它是我的组成部分。

782
00:39:41.770 --> 00:39:43.730
Without it, I would not be me.
没有它，我就不再是我了。

783
00:39:44.150 --> 00:39:45.750
And I like me.
而我很喜欢现在的自己。

784
00:39:46.570 --> 00:39:51.610
Down Syndrome is a genetic condition where you have an
唐氏综合征是一种基因疾病，意味着你拥有一个

785
00:39:51.610 --> 00:39:52.830
extra chromosome.
额外的染色体。

786
00:39:53.270 --> 00:39:59.810
And what the extra chromosome does is it holds in all the extra awesome.
而这个额外的染色体起到的作用，就是把所有爆棚的酷劲都装在里面。

787
00:40:00.570 --> 00:40:01.950
Normal people
正常人

788
00:40:01.950 --> 00:40:05.110
can't hold in all their awesome.
根本兜不住他们身上所有的酷劲。

789
00:40:05.510 --> 00:40:06.950
It leaks out.
它都溢出来了。

790
00:40:07.230 --> 00:40:10.590
But my awesome, it stays right in there.
但我的酷劲，它就好好地呆在里面。

791
00:40:11.010 --> 00:40:12.430
That's why I'm such
这就是为什么我这么

792
00:40:12.430 --> 00:40:13.810
a positive dude.
积极乐观。

793
00:40:14.030 --> 00:40:15.550
And everybody loves me.
而且每个人都喜欢我。

794
00:40:15.950 --> 00:40:17.490
That's just facts.
这都是不争的事实。

795
00:40:18.350 --> 00:40:20.910
There are lots of parts to me.
我的身上有很多面。

796
00:40:21.610 --> 00:40:23.210
I love poor jam.
我喜欢果酱。

797
00:40:23.570 --> 00:40:31.210
I play druMs. My dad used to play druMs. And he taught me how to play too,
我打架子鼓。我爸爸以前也打架子鼓。他也教过我怎么打，

798
00:40:31.530 --> 00:40:33.710
using our 90s rock.
伴着我们九十年代的摇滚乐。

799
00:40:34.190 --> 00:40:38.350
I am a better drummer than my dad now.
我现在打鼓比我爸还厉害。

800
00:40:38.890 --> 00:40:43.430
I can play along to almost all of
我几乎能跟上所有

801
00:40:43.430 --> 00:40:45.230
poor jam's songs.
Poor Jam 的歌曲。

802
00:40:45.510 --> 00:40:51.410
Well, at least the ones I like beSt. My sister says,
好吧，至少是我最喜欢的那些。我姐姐说，

803
00:40:51.610 --> 00:40:56.510
you let dad brainwash you into liking dad rock.
你被老爸洗脑了，才会喜欢老爸摇滚。

804
00:40:56.770 --> 00:41:01.790
But maybe it's just amazing music.
但也许这只是极好的音乐。

805
00:41:02.270 --> 00:41:05.130
And dad was right to brainwash me.
而且老爸洗脑我并没有错。

806
00:41:05.810 --> 00:41:08.870
I graduated from high school.
我高中毕业了。

807
00:41:09.170 --> 00:41:12.510
Then I graduated from my life skills
然后我从生活技能

808
00:41:12.510 --> 00:41:13.030
program.
项目毕业了。

809
00:41:13.410 --> 00:41:15.190
I have a job.
我有工作。

810
00:41:15.410 --> 00:41:20.550
I have a house I live in with a few of my friends from the program.
我和项目里的几个朋友合租了一栋房子。

811
00:41:20.550 --> 00:41:23.030
Sydney, Petey, and Elise.
悉尼、皮蒂和爱丽丝。

812
00:41:23.530 --> 00:41:28.810
And our great direct support peeps are there a lot to help out.
我们的优秀直属支持人员也经常来帮忙。

813
00:41:29.550 --> 00:41:33.730
Most important, I have a girlfriend, Amy.
最重要的是，我有一个女朋友，艾米。

814
00:41:34.290 --> 00:41:37.010
She is the love of my life.
她是我一生的挚爱。

815
00:41:37.370 --> 00:41:41.110
Our song is Release by Poor Jam.
我们的定情曲是 Poor Jam 的《Release》。

816
00:41:41.110 --> 00:41:42.010
My mom.
我妈妈。

817
00:41:42.010 --> 00:41:44.150
We listen to it all the time.
我们随时都在听。

818
00:41:44.790 --> 00:41:48.510
We kiss each other when we listen to that song.
听那首歌时我们会接吻。

819
00:41:48.950 --> 00:41:50.950
Even if we are not
即使我们不

820
00:41:50.950 --> 00:41:51.350
together.
在一起。

821
00:41:51.750 --> 00:41:55.050
We call each other and listen to that song.
我们会打电话一起听那首歌。

822
00:41:56.090 --> 00:42:00.250
All this good stuff is because of my family.
这一切美好的事物都要归功于我的家人。

823
00:42:00.250 --> 00:42:09.270
They are the beSt. My mom worked really hard to get me a job and a place to live.
他们是最棒的。我妈妈非常努力地帮我找工作和住所。

824
00:42:09.870 --> 00:42:12.090
My dad went away for work
我小时候，爸爸经常

825
00:42:12.090 --> 00:42:14.730
a lot when I was a kid.
出差工作。

826
00:42:14.990 --> 00:42:16.990
But I know he loves me.
但我知道他爱我。

827
00:42:17.490 --> 00:42:22.350
My younger sister, Darcy, is always there for me.
我小妹达西总是陪着我。

828
00:42:22.350 --> 00:42:26.650
